[Music]  across the infinite cosmos of the video  game no man's sky  there are a similarly infinite number of  alien life forms  through the use of procedural generation  the game contains more than 18  quintillion planets to discover many of  which team with extraordinary creatures  while no man's sky had a rocky reception  at launch the developers have done  persistent work making this virtual  universe worth exploring  so for this entry into the archive  we'll embark on a classic documentary  style expedition  exploring the lives of extraterrestrials  on scorching worlds frozen wastelands  and many others i'll also speculate on  how the biology of each life form might  feasibly work i admit that there are a  few too many total planets for this  archivist to document so this  documentary will focus on only the most  interesting ones i've discovered  now let's head off into the unknown and  see what awaits us among the stars  we'll begin with an earth-like temperate  world located a comfortable distance  from its host star  since we are the first explorers to ever  witness this planet it's up to us to  come up with a name we'll call this ring  jewel of the cosmos planet rhea a land  abundant with the promise of discovery  entering the atmosphere near the equator  we can see a vast landscape of green  fields stretching before us under the  orbiting rings above who knows what  extraterrestrial life has emerged  stepping out of the spacecraft i spot  something moving in the distance a herd  of herbivorous giants are grazing on the  local vegetation  these newly discovered creatures also  need a name we'll call them titano  magnus magnificus which might be a bit  much but i'm excited the titano magnus  seem to have converged upon a niche  similar to sauropod dinosaurs from  earth's past they survive by being too  large for most predators to bother with  and sustain their bulk by vacuuming up  over one ton of plant matter each day  with their long necks and curious ears  the titano magnus actually resemble  another earth animal the giraffe a life  form whose long neck helps them reach  leaves at the tops of trees yet there  are no trees in this region of planet  rhea so why bother with such a long neck  perhaps a tree like genus recently went  extinct or perhaps the necks serve as  watchtowers to keep an eye out for  potential dangers  and speaking of potential dangers a huge  armored predator is on the move i'll  call these unfriendly customers the  arachnomantis because well i can the  arachnomantis possess a bone-crushing  beak and seem to have some kind of  exoskeleton the biological differences  between the arachnomantis and  titanomagnus seem so extreme i wonder if  like land vertebrates and insects here  on earth these two terrestrial lineages  split off long before crawling onto land  yet unlike insects the arachnomantis are  megafauna in their own right and a  serious danger upon these planes  with our different evolutionary origins  it's likely i wouldn't be very tasty to  an arachnomantis but it's best not to  test that theory  for the next leg of our voyage across  planet rhea will be traveling in a  terrestrial exocraft called a roamer  this vehicle will offer protection as we  continue to explore this unfamiliar land  plus it's nice to not have to walk for  the entire voyage  not far from our roamer something is  disturbing the grass  this is a crested railope these  diminutive grazers are difficult to get  a glimpse of as they've learned their  best chance of survival in this world of  giants is to stay out of sight their  skittish behavior likens them to the  antelopes of the grasslands here on  earth we're lucky to be able to get a  sighting of such a shy creature  but railopes aren't the only things  hiding in the grass even more elusive  are the shadowy striped dread tooth  these cat-like hunters are exceedingly  difficult to spot  like tigers their unique pattern of  stripes help them blend into their  environment and the spines on their back  help them disappear even further and  this dread tooth has caught the scent of  something typically dread tooth feed  only on rayalopes and the youngest of  titano magnus but this dread tooth has  its sights on an adult we might have a  serious fight on our hands the dread  tooth circles in close  then seems to think better of it a  full-grown titanomagness isn't exactly  an easy target it's just not worth the  risk and so the dreadtooth returns to  the prowl looking for something a little  smaller to snack on  the sun is now setting on planet rhea  yet with the night comes a final  surprise the arachnomantis while a  fearsome predator during the daylight  lights up the dark with a bioluminescent  display as it calls out to others of its  kind this ritual which might be for  mating purposes is a touching one for  such a deadly creature we've seen much  during our travels across planet rhea  but now the stars call us once again  this world is just one of many and the  moment has come to continue our  expedition  the next stop on our voyage planet  bereas lies on the outer edge of its  star's habitable zone  entering the atmosphere i find a land  trapped in a never-ending winter berea's  position combined with a dim host star  means temperature on the surface rarely  rises above freezing  and a layer of snow and ice covers the  surface year round it's not the sort of  place one might expect to find life  yet life is here all the same this is a  snow snuffler a life form perfectly  adapted for a sub-zero lifestyle  large lumbering herbivores they're  protected from the cold thanks to a  thick layer of fat and insulating fur  wrapping oneself in the biological  equivalent of a thick winter coat is one  of the most common ways that animals  here on earth have been able to conquer  cold environments  so it makes sense the snow snufflers  would have a convergent tactic for  staying warm but surviving the elements  is only half the battle to persist on  planet bereas the snow snufflers must  also find food  luckily this is something the snow  snuffler is quite good at their  sensitive trunks are equipped with scent  receptors powerful enough to locate the  subterranean vegetation the snow  snufflers feed upon so the snow  snufflers have sniffed their way into an  enviable spot on the food web  but there's more than one way to survive  on a planet of ice horned chillmanders  are scaly creatures that aren't as well  insulated from the cold and aren't as  proficient at sniffing out food instead  they have a different strategy to  confront the low temperatures  hibernation  on earth numerous animals hibernate  during winter months slowing their  metabolic rate to conserve energy only  to emerge again when food is more  abundant on planet bereas however  temperatures drop without warning year  round which is why the chillmanders are  capable of slowing their metabolic rate  multiple times per year these lethargic  life forms spend most of their time  basking in the sun expending precious  little energy even when not hibernating  it's a lifestyle i'm a bit jealous of  even if it's not the most exciting  yet where there are herbivores  particularly abundant slow moving ones  there are invariably carnivores lumber  moths are tall somewhat awkward looking  predators that spend most of their time  reared up on their hind legs to  intimidate rivals and survey the  landscape while they are the dominant  predators of this region lumber moths  aren't particularly aggressive  like many species of bears they are  hypocarnivorous meaning their diet  consists mainly of fungi berries in  other plant materials rather than meat  after all on a planet as harsh as bereas  being picky just isn't practical i'm not  entirely certain if they'd like the  taste of me so i'll give them some  personal space planet bereas is an  extreme and fascinating world but the  time has come to continue our voyage  our next galactic destination is planet  nehrus home to an incredible planet-wide  ocean  entering the atmosphere i find that only  a few small islands break up the endless  expanse of water most life on planet  nehrus is likely waiting under the waves  yet touching down on one of the larger  islands i find some intrepid species  have come ashore at the water's edge i  spot a coastal shell swimmer amphibious  herbivores shell swimmers feed off  marine plants that grow in the shallows  just beyond the shore it's a lifestyle  similar to the marine iguanas of the  galapagos islands which likewise spend  most of their life span in the  intertidal zone on planet nehrus even  land dwellers are tied to the sea  elsewhere on the island the bizarre glow  horns feed on coastal swamp grass in  appearance and behavior glow horns are  convergent with hoofed ruminant mammals  like deer yet when night falls these  lifeforms reveal a side that is all  their own bioluminescent display  structures on their back light up  creating a dazzling display that helps  the glow horns find potential mates in  the darkness it's a mesmerizing  spectacle to see in person  yet the light of glow horns can attract  more than potential mates it can also  attract predators and on the island  coast no predator is more dangerous than  the terror beak these t-rex like  creatures are huge towering over all  other land animals on these islands it  might seem surprising to see large  creatures in an isolated ecosystem yet  this is actually an example of island  gigantism a trend that exists on earth  as well in species like komodo dragons  island gigantism is a biological  phenomenon in which a species on an  island increases dramatically in size  for the terabeaks their massive bulk  allows them to feed on any species they  wish  yet land animals only make up a small  percentage of life on nehru's diving  under the waves i find a much denser  ecosystem awaits the first life forms i  spot are the inquisitive tentacled  cephalophores that move in sporadic  patterns in accordance to the ocean  currents cephalophores travel in groups  perhaps for protection or perhaps  because they just like the company their  soft bodies and manipulatory tentacles  resemble those of an octopus and like  octopuses they're quite intelligent  exactly how intelligent is difficult to  measure but they show an acute sense of  curiosity circling around me as i swim  by i wonder if perhaps the cephalophores  feel they are studying me  the bulk of underwater species within  the planet-wide ocean are fast-moving  fish-like life-forms we'll call silver  fins they gather in schools that number  in the thousands much like the true fish  of our oceans and with such high numbers  silver fins are an appealing food source  for aquatic predators  in one such predator is lurking below  this silent streamlined hunter is a  saltwater reef stalker the premier  hunter of this global ocean reef  stalkers are significantly faster than  their preferred prey using their  muscular tail to propel themselves  through the water their torpedo-like  body plan mirrors that of most sharks as  does their killer appetite in these  bountiful waters every day is a feast  yet fortunately like earth sharks this  reef stalker ultimately isn't that  interested in taking a bite out of me  all the same i'd feel safer with some  extra protection to explore the deepest  region of this global ocean i'm  traveling in an aquatic exocraft called  anatolon  at the bottom of the largest trench on  planet nehrus something mysterious is  waiting a bright light emanates from the  eye of a strange organism growing from a  wall exiting my submarine i move in  closer only to be caught in a hypnotic  vortex of light it takes all my strength  to break away  that was an abyssal horror a lifeform  that calls to prey with a bioluminescent  lure much like an earth anglerfish  i suddenly feel that i've seen enough of  planet nerus  racing along through the stars i find my  ship is low on fuel  fortunately i know just the place to get  some more this strange geometric  construction is a space station a common  sight in this part of the cosmos they  function almost like intergalactic truck  stops and are open to all kinds of  space-faring life  as our ship enters the space station  through the main aperture the automatic  guiding system takes over and we're  ushered towards the first available  landing pad after so much time exploring  the cosmic wilds it's a strange  sensation to return to an artificial  environment yet we need fuel to continue  our expedition so we might as well relax  this station is run by the diminutive  geck one of the primary sentient species  in this region of space they're  organized and rather pragmatic beings  more interested in practical matters  than conversation  while i'd like to know more about the  specifics of their biology i've yet to  meet a gek comfortable with discussing  that topic so i won't press it all sorts  of different species pass through this  particular station  some like the mysterious corvax appear  to be entirely artificial how these  inorganic life forms function is of  particular interest but like the geck  they aren't keen on sharing secrets  still just being in the presence of  other intelligent life forms some of  which are likely explorers themselves is  a special privilege but with the ship  refueled the time is right to return to  our voyage  the second to last planet we'll be  visiting is the most extreme so far  planet helios orbits extremely close to  its star making it a world of blistering  temperatures  entering the atmosphere a sun-scorched  landscape of ash and smoke awaits  only a few barren plants are able to  take root in this infernal biosphere  i don't expect to find much life here  but life is nothing if not stubborn a  few persistent organisms have risen to  the challenge the most tenacious  creatures we'll call igneo beasts  forms with a curious defense against the  heat like the sea pangolins of the  indian ocean they incorporate mineral  sulfides into their hide like a kind of  fire resistant second skin  allowing igneobeast to survive in this  volcanic wasteland igneous beasts are  also excellent tunnelers allowing them  to dig for edible roots and underground  aquifers it's an extreme life but a life  all the same  and speaking of extreme  [Music]  that was a heliostrider a titanic  lifeform with a body plan unlike any  organism i've ever come across their  alarming height means that helio  striders pay little mind to anything on  this planet's surface like igneo beasts  these omnivores feed primarily on buried  plant matter sticking their heads  underground to get a meal it's a  somewhat awkward behavior that calls to  mind how ostriches look when burying  their eggs  like most life forms on planet helios  the skin of the heliostrider seems  highly resistant to the merciless solar  radiation in fact the helio striders are  practically thriving  but not all creatures on planet helios  are quite so fortunate  crag spines are mid-sized scavengers  that struggle to find sustenance in this  barren environment at a glance they  resemble the savannah foxes of our  planet although the niche they occupy is  less enviable  crag spines live short sweaty lives  under the uncaring sun rarely getting  enough food to stave off hunger a harsh  existence for a harsh world planet  helios has shown us the incredible  tenacity of life but now let's head to  our final planet  at the end of our journey through the  stars the massive mysterious planet  erebuzz awaits from our current position  it's impossible to tell what the surface  looks like entering the atmosphere and  flying below the clouds i discover a  hidden paradise is waiting with a  temperate climate in abundant vegetation  planet erebuzz is a place where  evolution is free to experiment like  never before  and here is one such experiment now  my goodness  this is a well it's difficult to think  of a name i'll call them  george  the georges appear to be herbivores with  mouths located on the underside of their  bodies to feed georges simply move  across the rich carpet of vegetation  that covers the planet essentially  functioning like living lawn mowers  their system of locomotion is comparable  to terrestrial snails which slowly  propel themselves using waves of  muscular contractions  dozens of primitive eyes cover the front  end of the georges which might seem like  overkill yet certain types of scallops  on our own planet are known to have an  even higher total eye count it's easy to  dismiss the georges as some sort of  biological misadventure yet all forms of  life no matter how bizarre or their own  sort of miracle  in the skies above planet arabs  something remarkable is passing overhead  these are aereoderms of remarkable form  of floating life they're held aloft by  some kind of internal gas bladder their  trunks aren't quite as impressive as  those of an elephant and are perhaps  more analogous to the schwart prehensile  noses of tapers yet erioderms can feed  on the tops of trees as their buoyant  bodies mean nothing is out of reach  for the last leg of my journey across  planet erebuzz i'll be using a special  research vehicle  this exocraft is called a minotaur a  robust mechanical walker that allows me  to travel further and stay safer  and it seems that extra precautions  weren't a mistake a horrifying mass of  tentacles burst from the ground grasping  at the air close to me this subterranean  terror cannot be seen in full so i'll  simply call them nightmares  without being able to see the rest of  these life forms it is impossible to  determine their exact biology but they  seem to be ambush predators that burrow  under their targets and attack from  below even a paradise like erebuzz can  be a dangerous place to linger  yet with the night a deep calm settles  over this normally restless planet it is  a bittersweet feeling to know our voyage  is complete but the time has come to  head for home  yet of course no man's sky is a game  without end beyond each horizon is  another one with every planet just a  fleeting waypoint in a voyage without a  destination  there's a certain melancholy that the  game can evoke as the sheer size of the  universe creeps into one's mind no  matter how long you spend in this  universe on a cosmic scale there is only  so much a single entity can do and see  i think the team behind this project  have done an admirable job expanding  this procedural universe and i'm excited  to know what comes next  and as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support by liking subscribing and  hitting the notification icon to stay up  to date on all things curious  see you in the next video  you

